  user_input {
    user_response: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the html this is the copy f\n# Orji Munachi \342\200\224 Portfolio Website\n## Complete Copy & Build Instructions for AI Agent\n\n---\n\n## OVERVIEW & BRIEF\n\n**Client:** Orji Munachi\n**Email:** orjimunachi5@gmail.com\n**Role:** Full-Package Social Media Manager\n**Goal:** Convert visitors into paying freelance clients. This website acts as a resume/CV. No pricing displayed anywhere on the site.\n**Target Clients:** Physical businesses \342\200\224 fashion labels, car dealerships, agribusinesses\n**Tone:** First-person, confident, direct. No em dashes. No emojis. No generic AI copy.\n**Conversion Target:** 2 to 3 out of 10 visitors should take action (click Hire Me or send an email)\n\n---\n\n## DESIGN INSTRUCTIONS (Global)\n\n- Branding: colors, fonts, and visual identity to be supplied by client after completion of brand visuals. Do not apply any default branding.\n- No stock photography anywhere on the site.\n- Tool logos in the Skills section must be real SVG logos \342\200\224 Canva, CapCut, Meta, TikTok, Google Ads, Meta Business Suite, Google Analytics, Buffer, Hootsuite. Not text labels, not generic icons.\n- Case study cards: use a clean industry icon if no real brand logo is provided \342\200\224 a car for Opara Motors, a crop/leaf for Omereugu Farms, a building for Zext Ventures.\n- Real mockups or screenshots can be inserted by the client before launch. Leave clearly labeled placeholder slots where indicated.\n- Navigation is sticky. All nav links scroll smoothly to their sections.\n- The primary CTA button \"Hire Me\" must appear in the nav, the hero, and the final CTA section.\n- No pricing anywhere on the site.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1 \342\200\224 HERO\n\n**Section ID:** hero\n\n**Name displayed:**\nOrji Munachi\n\n**Tagline (largest text on the page):**\nThe only social media hire you need.\n\n**Subheadline:**\nI handle your strategy, content, ads, and analytics \342\200\224 so you stop juggling freelancers and start seeing results.\n\n**Supporting Line:**\nI work with physical businesses: fashion labels, car dealerships, agribusinesses, and the brands that sell real things to real people.\n\n**Primary CTA Button:**\nHire Me\n(links to final CTA section or opens email client to orjimunachi5@gmail.com)\n\n**Secondary CTA:**\nSee My Work\n(smooth scrolls to Case Studies section)\n\n**Design Note:**\nDisplay three proof stats beside or below the headline as bold numbers:\n- 10,000+ Views Generated\n- 3 Industries Served\n- 3 Paying Clients\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nThe tagline makes a bold claim that triggers curiosity. The subheadline immediately answers how. The supporting line filters the right clients in and the wrong ones out. The Hire Me button is direct with no softening language.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2 \342\200\224 ABOUT\n\n**Section ID:** about\n\n**Section Label:**\nAbout Me\n\n**Headline:**\nI don\'t just manage social media. I build the online presence your business deserves.\n\n**Body Copy:**\n\nMy name is Munachi. I\'m a social media manager with a full toolkit and a simple promise: you hire one person, you get everything done properly.\n\nI design the visuals. I write the copy. I edit the videos. I build and run the ads. I track the numbers and tell you what they mean. Most of my clients came to me after burning money on disconnected freelancers who couldn\'t see the full picture. I see the full picture.\n\nI work best with businesses that sell physical things: the fashion brand trying to move product, the car dealership that thinks social media isn\'t for them, the agribusiness ready to build a real audience. I understand how to make tangible things feel desirable online, and I know how to turn that desire into action.\n\nI\'m not the cheapest option. I\'m the one that works.\n\n**Design Note:**\nLeft side: copy. Right side: professional photo of Munachi (placeholder slot \342\200\224 client to supply before launch). If no photo is provided at build time, use a clean geometric placeholder with her initials. Do not use stock photography of a random person.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nOpens by reframing expectations. The paragraph listing what she does reads as a checklist a frustrated client mentally ticks. \"Burning money on disconnected freelancers\" names their exact pain before they name it. The final line pre-qualifies budget-conscious enquiries and positions her as premium without quoting a price.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3 \342\200\224 SERVICES\n\n**Section ID:** services\n\n**Section Label:**\nWhat I Do\n\n**Headline:**\nEverything your brand needs to win on social media. Nothing you don\'t.\n\n**Subline:**\nI offer six core services. Most clients start with two or three and add the rest once they see results.\n\n---\n\n**Service 1**\nTitle: Strategy and Planning\nCopy: Before a single post goes live, we build a plan. I audit your current presence, study your competitors, identify your audience, and map out a content direction that aligns with your business goals. You stop posting randomly and start posting with purpose.\n\n**Service 2**\nTitle: Content Creation\nCopy: I create content that looks like it belongs on the feed of a brand three times your size. Graphics, carousels, short-form video, long-form video \342\200\224 designed in Canva, edited in CapCut. Every piece made to stop the scroll.\n\n**Service 3**\nTitle: Copywriting\nCopy: The visuals stop them. The words make them act. I write captions, ad copy, content scripts, and campaign messaging that sells without sounding like it is selling. Whether the goal is awareness, education, or conversion, the writing earns its place.\n\n**Service 4**\nTitle: Paid Ads Management\nCopy: I plan, build, and manage ad campaigns across Meta, TikTok, and Google. Audience targeting, creative testing, budget management, and performance optimisation. Your money goes further because every decision is backed by data, not guesswork.\n\n**Service 5**\nTitle: Analytics and Reporting\nCopy: I track what matters and ignore what doesn\'t. Every month you get a clear report \342\200\224 what worked, what didn\'t, what we do next. No vanity metrics, no confusion. Just honest numbers and a direction forward.\n\n**Service 6**\nTitle: Community Management\nCopy: Your audience is talking. I make sure your brand is listening and responding in a way that builds loyalty, not just follower counts. I manage your DMs, comments, and community interactions so your brand always shows up professionally.\n\n**Design Note:**\nSix cards in a 3x2 grid. Each card has a clean industry-relevant icon at the top, the service title in bold, and the copy beneath in a lighter weight. Cards have a subtle border and a hover state that lifts them slightly. No pricing on any card.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nThe subline \"most clients start with two or three\" lowers the entry barrier and removes the pressure of committing to everything at once. Each service leads with the outcome the client gets, not the task being performed.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4 \342\200\224 SKILLS AND TOOLS\n\n**Section ID:** skills\n\n**Section Label:**\nSkills and Tools\n\n**Headline:**\nI come equipped. No learning on the job.\n\n**Subline:**\nEvery tool I use, I use properly. Every skill I list, I can prove.\n\n---\n\n**SKILLS \342\200\224 Four Pillars**\n\nDisplay as four bold cards or columns.\n\nPillar 1 \342\200\224 Creative Production\nGraphic design, video editing, short-form content, long-form content, carousel design, brand visuals.\n\nPillar 2 \342\200\224 Strategy and Planning\nContent strategy, platform auditing, competitor research, audience profiling, content calendars, trend analysis, brand voice development.\n\nPillar 3 \342\200\224 Paid Advertising\nCampaign setup, audience targeting, A/B creative testing, budget optimisation, retargeting, conversion tracking, ad copywriting.\n\nPillar 4 \342\200\224 Analytics and Reporting\nPerformance tracking, KPI reporting, engagement analysis, reach and impression reporting, ROI measurement, monthly strategy reviews.\n\n---\n\n**TOOLS \342\200\224 By Category**\n\nDisplay with real SVG logos. Not text. Not generic icons. Real logos.\n\nDesign and Content Creation:\n- Canva (logo)\n- CapCut (logo)\n\nSocial Media Platforms:\n- Instagram (logo)\n- Facebook (logo)\n- TikTok (logo)\n- LinkedIn (logo)\n- X / Twitter (logo)\n- YouTube (logo)\n\nPaid Advertising:\n- Meta Ads Manager (logo)\n- TikTok Ads Manager (logo)\n- Google Ads (logo)\n\nAnalytics and Reporting:\n- Meta Business Suite (logo)\n- Google Analytics (logo)\n- TikTok Analytics (logo)\n\nScheduling and Management:\n- Buffer (logo)\n- Hootsuite (logo)\n\n**Design Note:**\nTop half of section: four skill pillars as cards in a row. Bottom half: tool logos displayed in a clean horizontal logo strip grouped by category.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\n\"No learning on the job\" directly addresses a real client fear \342\200\224 paying someone to figure things out at their expense. Real logos signal daily professional use. Four pillars make breadth feel structured rather than scattered.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5 \342\200\224 CASE STUDIES\n\n**Section ID:** work\n\n**Section Label:**\nMy Work\n\n**Headline:**\nReal businesses. Real results.\n\n**Subline:**\nEvery brand I have worked with sells something physical. Here is what happened when they trusted me with their social media.\n\n---\n\n**Case Study 1 \342\200\224 Opara Motors**\nIndustry Tag: Automotive\nIcon: Car icon (or Opara Motors logo if supplied by client)\nServices Delivered: Content creation, video editing, social media management\n\nCard Headline:\nA car dealership that finally looked the part online.\n\nBody Copy:\nOpara Motors came to me with a social media presence that didn\'t reflect the quality of what they were selling. In one month, I took over their content \342\200\224 scripting, shooting direction, editing, and posting \342\200\224 and built a consistent visual identity around their inventory.\n\nThe result: 8,405 views, 6,722 people reached, and 1,000 new followers. In 30 days. For a car dealership that previously had next to no traction online.\n\nWhen your product costs what a car costs, your content needs to match that value. That was the brief. That was the result.\n\nMetrics (display as a 2x2 stat grid at the bottom of the card):\n- 8,405 Views\n- 6,722 Reach\n- 1,000 New Followers\n- 30 Days\n\n---\n\n**Case Study 2 \342\200\224 Omereugu Farms**\nIndustry Tag: Agriculture\nIcon: Crop or leaf icon (or brand logo if supplied by client)\nServices Delivered: Social media management, copywriting, video editing, strategic content\n\nCard Headline:\nBuilt from nothing. On purpose.\n\nBody Copy:\nOmereugu Farms had no social media presence at all. No followers, no content, no strategy. I built everything from the ground up \342\200\224 the content direction, the brand voice, the posting rhythm, the visual identity.\n\nStarting from zero is harder than it looks. There is no existing audience to lean on, no past content to learn from. Every follower is earned. We grew their TikTok to 50 followers and their Instagram to 12, with over 3,000 views across platforms in the early stages.\n\nThese are foundation numbers. What they represent is a brand that now exists online, speaks consistently, and is growing. The work here was not just execution \342\200\224 it was architecture.\n\nMetrics (display as a 2x2 stat grid at the bottom of the card):\n- 3,000+ Views\n- 50 TikTok Followers\n- 12 Instagram Followers\n- Built from 0\n\n---\n\n**Case Study 3 \342\200\224 Zext Ventures**\nIndustry Tag: Business Services\nIcon: Building icon (or brand logo if supplied by client)\nServices Delivered: Social media management, copywriting, video editing\n\nCard Headline:\nConsistent presence. Professional voice. Every week.\n\nBody Copy:\nZext Ventures needed a social media presence that matched the seriousness of their business. My job was to show up consistently, maintain a professional brand voice, and produce content that positioned them credibly in their space.\n\nOver two months I managed their platforms end to end \342\200\224 content creation, copy, video editing, and scheduling. 543 views and over 100 followers gained in a competitive space where most business service brands struggle to get any organic traction at all.\n\nNot every client needs to go viral. Some need to simply show up, look credible, and build steadily. That is exactly what we did.\n\nMetrics (display as a 2x2 stat grid at the bottom of the card):\n- 543 Views\n- 100+ New Followers\n- 2 Months\n- 3 Platforms\n\n---\n\n**Design Note:**\nThree cards side by side. Each card has the industry tag small at the top, the headline large, body copy in a lighter weight, and the 2x2 metric grid at the bottom. If the client supplies real screenshots or content mockups from these projects, display them as a visual thumbnail at the top of each card. If not, use the industry icon only. Do not fabricate mockup images.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nEach case study tells a deliberately different story. Opara Motors is speed and impact. Omereugu Farms is about building from nothing, which positions Munachi as someone trusted at a brand\'s most vulnerable stage. Zext Ventures reframes modest numbers as intentional consistency. Together the three signal range across industries without undermining each other.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6 \342\200\224 TESTIMONIALS\n\n**Section ID:** testimonials\n\n**Section Label:**\nWhat Clients Say\n\n**Headline:**\nDon\'t take my word for it.\n\n---\n\n**Testimonial Card 1**\nAvatar: Initials placeholder circle\nClient Name: [Opara Motors Client Name \342\200\224 to be filled before launch]\nRole: [Owner / Manager, Opara Motors]\nQuote: [Client quote to be inserted by Munachi before launch]\n\n**Testimonial Card 2**\nAvatar: Initials placeholder circle\nClient Name: [Omereugu Farms Client Name \342\200\224 to be filled before launch]\nRole: [Owner / Manager, Omereugu Farms]\nQuote: [Client quote to be inserted by Munachi before launch]\n\n**Testimonial Card 3**\nAvatar: Initials placeholder circle\nClient Name: [Zext Ventures Client Name \342\200\224 to be filled before launch]\nRole: [Owner / Manager, Zext Ventures]\nQuote: [Client quote to be inserted by Munachi before launch]\n\n**Design Note:**\nThree cards side by side. Each card has a large opening quotation mark, the quote text in italics at a lighter weight, client name in bold below, and their role in a smaller muted size beneath that. Leave an avatar circle for a headshot \342\200\224 use initials if no photo is provided. Do not fabricate any quote content. Placeholder text must be clearly marked for the client to replace before the site goes live.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7 \342\200\224 FINAL CTA\n\n**Section ID:** contact\n\n**Section Label:**\nLet\'s Work\n\n**Headline:**\nYou\'ve seen the work. You know what I do. Let\'s talk about what I can do for you.\n\n**Body Copy:**\nI take on a limited number of clients at a time so every brand I work with gets my full attention. If you are a physical business that is serious about social media, I want to hear from you.\n\n**Primary CTA Button:**\nHire Me\n(opens email client to orjimunachi5@gmail.com)\n\n**Secondary Line beneath button (smaller, muted):**\nor email me directly at orjimunachi5@gmail.com\n\n**Design Note:**\nFull-width section. Headline centered. Button centered beneath copy. Email address beneath button as a plain clickable mailto link. No form. No contact form. Direct email only \342\200\224 lowest possible friction.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\n\"Limited number of clients\" creates scarcity without being manipulative and signals that her time is genuinely in demand. \"Serious about social media\" filters out tyre-kickers and price shoppers. The email sitting beneath the button removes every possible barrier between a decision and an action.\n\n---\n\n## NAVIGATION\n\nSticky nav.\n\nLeft: Name \342\200\224 Orji Munachi\nRight links: About, Services, Skills, Work, Contact\nFar right: Hire Me button\n\nAll links smooth-scroll to their respective sections.\n\n---\n\n## FOOTER\n\nLeft: Orji Munachi, Social Media Manager, 2026\nCenter or right: orjimunachi5@gmail.com\nSocial links: Instagram, LinkedIn (placeholders \342\200\224 client to supply profile URLs before launch)\n\nNo pricing. No copyright notice needed beyond the year.\n\n---\n\n## PRE-LAUNCH CHECKLIST FOR MUNACHI\n\nBefore the site goes live, replace the following:\n\n1. Supply brand visuals \342\200\224 colors, fonts, logo \342\200\224 from Google Stitch for the agent to apply\n2. Professional photo in the About section\n3. All three testimonial quotes and client names\n4. Brand logos for Opara Motors, Omereugu Farms, and Zext Ventures (if available)\n5. Real content screenshots or mockups for case study cards (if available)\n6. Instagram and LinkedIn profile URLs in the footer\n7. Confirm the Hire Me button correctly opens orjimunachi5@gmail.com\n\n---\n\n*Document prepared for AI agent handoff. All copy is final. Design notes are instructions, not suggestions. Branding to be applied by client after Google Stitch visuals are ready.*"
    items {
      text: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can hotlink images from the html this is the copy f\n# Orji Munachi \342\200\224 Portfolio Website\n## Complete Copy & Build Instructions for AI Agent\n\n---\n\n## OVERVIEW & BRIEF\n\n**Client:** Orji Munachi\n**Email:** orjimunachi5@gmail.com\n**Role:** Full-Package Social Media Manager\n**Goal:** Convert visitors into paying freelance clients. This website acts as a resume/CV. No pricing displayed anywhere on the site.\n**Target Clients:** Physical businesses \342\200\224 fashion labels, car dealerships, agribusinesses\n**Tone:** First-person, confident, direct. No em dashes. No emojis. No generic AI copy.\n**Conversion Target:** 2 to 3 out of 10 visitors should take action (click Hire Me or send an email)\n\n---\n\n## DESIGN INSTRUCTIONS (Global)\n\n- Branding: colors, fonts, and visual identity to be supplied by client after completion of brand visuals. Do not apply any default branding.\n- No stock photography anywhere on the site.\n- Tool logos in the Skills section must be real SVG logos \342\200\224 Canva, CapCut, Meta, TikTok, Google Ads, Meta Business Suite, Google Analytics, Buffer, Hootsuite. Not text labels, not generic icons.\n- Case study cards: use a clean industry icon if no real brand logo is provided \342\200\224 a car for Opara Motors, a crop/leaf for Omereugu Farms, a building for Zext Ventures.\n- Real mockups or screenshots can be inserted by the client before launch. Leave clearly labeled placeholder slots where indicated.\n- Navigation is sticky. All nav links scroll smoothly to their sections.\n- The primary CTA button \"Hire Me\" must appear in the nav, the hero, and the final CTA section.\n- No pricing anywhere on the site.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 1 \342\200\224 HERO\n\n**Section ID:** hero\n\n**Name displayed:**\nOrji Munachi\n\n**Tagline (largest text on the page):**\nThe only social media hire you need.\n\n**Subheadline:**\nI handle your strategy, content, ads, and analytics \342\200\224 so you stop juggling freelancers and start seeing results.\n\n**Supporting Line:**\nI work with physical businesses: fashion labels, car dealerships, agribusinesses, and the brands that sell real things to real people.\n\n**Primary CTA Button:**\nHire Me\n(links to final CTA section or opens email client to orjimunachi5@gmail.com)\n\n**Secondary CTA:**\nSee My Work\n(smooth scrolls to Case Studies section)\n\n**Design Note:**\nDisplay three proof stats beside or below the headline as bold numbers:\n- 10,000+ Views Generated\n- 3 Industries Served\n- 3 Paying Clients\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nThe tagline makes a bold claim that triggers curiosity. The subheadline immediately answers how. The supporting line filters the right clients in and the wrong ones out. The Hire Me button is direct with no softening language.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 2 \342\200\224 ABOUT\n\n**Section ID:** about\n\n**Section Label:**\nAbout Me\n\n**Headline:**\nI don\'t just manage social media. I build the online presence your business deserves.\n\n**Body Copy:**\n\nMy name is Munachi. I\'m a social media manager with a full toolkit and a simple promise: you hire one person, you get everything done properly.\n\nI design the visuals. I write the copy. I edit the videos. I build and run the ads. I track the numbers and tell you what they mean. Most of my clients came to me after burning money on disconnected freelancers who couldn\'t see the full picture. I see the full picture.\n\nI work best with businesses that sell physical things: the fashion brand trying to move product, the car dealership that thinks social media isn\'t for them, the agribusiness ready to build a real audience. I understand how to make tangible things feel desirable online, and I know how to turn that desire into action.\n\nI\'m not the cheapest option. I\'m the one that works.\n\n**Design Note:**\nLeft side: copy. Right side: professional photo of Munachi (placeholder slot \342\200\224 client to supply before launch). If no photo is provided at build time, use a clean geometric placeholder with her initials. Do not use stock photography of a random person.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nOpens by reframing expectations. The paragraph listing what she does reads as a checklist a frustrated client mentally ticks. \"Burning money on disconnected freelancers\" names their exact pain before they name it. The final line pre-qualifies budget-conscious enquiries and positions her as premium without quoting a price.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 3 \342\200\224 SERVICES\n\n**Section ID:** services\n\n**Section Label:**\nWhat I Do\n\n**Headline:**\nEverything your brand needs to win on social media. Nothing you don\'t.\n\n**Subline:**\nI offer six core services. Most clients start with two or three and add the rest once they see results.\n\n---\n\n**Service 1**\nTitle: Strategy and Planning\nCopy: Before a single post goes live, we build a plan. I audit your current presence, study your competitors, identify your audience, and map out a content direction that aligns with your business goals. You stop posting randomly and start posting with purpose.\n\n**Service 2**\nTitle: Content Creation\nCopy: I create content that looks like it belongs on the feed of a brand three times your size. Graphics, carousels, short-form video, long-form video \342\200\224 designed in Canva, edited in CapCut. Every piece made to stop the scroll.\n\n**Service 3**\nTitle: Copywriting\nCopy: The visuals stop them. The words make them act. I write captions, ad copy, content scripts, and campaign messaging that sells without sounding like it is selling. Whether the goal is awareness, education, or conversion, the writing earns its place.\n\n**Service 4**\nTitle: Paid Ads Management\nCopy: I plan, build, and manage ad campaigns across Meta, TikTok, and Google. Audience targeting, creative testing, budget management, and performance optimisation. Your money goes further because every decision is backed by data, not guesswork.\n\n**Service 5**\nTitle: Analytics and Reporting\nCopy: I track what matters and ignore what doesn\'t. Every month you get a clear report \342\200\224 what worked, what didn\'t, what we do next. No vanity metrics, no confusion. Just honest numbers and a direction forward.\n\n**Service 6**\nTitle: Community Management\nCopy: Your audience is talking. I make sure your brand is listening and responding in a way that builds loyalty, not just follower counts. I manage your DMs, comments, and community interactions so your brand always shows up professionally.\n\n**Design Note:**\nSix cards in a 3x2 grid. Each card has a clean industry-relevant icon at the top, the service title in bold, and the copy beneath in a lighter weight. Cards have a subtle border and a hover state that lifts them slightly. No pricing on any card.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nThe subline \"most clients start with two or three\" lowers the entry barrier and removes the pressure of committing to everything at once. Each service leads with the outcome the client gets, not the task being performed.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 4 \342\200\224 SKILLS AND TOOLS\n\n**Section ID:** skills\n\n**Section Label:**\nSkills and Tools\n\n**Headline:**\nI come equipped. No learning on the job.\n\n**Subline:**\nEvery tool I use, I use properly. Every skill I list, I can prove.\n\n---\n\n**SKILLS \342\200\224 Four Pillars**\n\nDisplay as four bold cards or columns.\n\nPillar 1 \342\200\224 Creative Production\nGraphic design, video editing, short-form content, long-form content, carousel design, brand visuals.\n\nPillar 2 \342\200\224 Strategy and Planning\nContent strategy, platform auditing, competitor research, audience profiling, content calendars, trend analysis, brand voice development.\n\nPillar 3 \342\200\224 Paid Advertising\nCampaign setup, audience targeting, A/B creative testing, budget optimisation, retargeting, conversion tracking, ad copywriting.\n\nPillar 4 \342\200\224 Analytics and Reporting\nPerformance tracking, KPI reporting, engagement analysis, reach and impression reporting, ROI measurement, monthly strategy reviews.\n\n---\n\n**TOOLS \342\200\224 By Category**\n\nDisplay with real SVG logos. Not text. Not generic icons. Real logos.\n\nDesign and Content Creation:\n- Canva (logo)\n- CapCut (logo)\n\nSocial Media Platforms:\n- Instagram (logo)\n- Facebook (logo)\n- TikTok (logo)\n- LinkedIn (logo)\n- X / Twitter (logo)\n- YouTube (logo)\n\nPaid Advertising:\n- Meta Ads Manager (logo)\n- TikTok Ads Manager (logo)\n- Google Ads (logo)\n\nAnalytics and Reporting:\n- Meta Business Suite (logo)\n- Google Analytics (logo)\n- TikTok Analytics (logo)\n\nScheduling and Management:\n- Buffer (logo)\n- Hootsuite (logo)\n\n**Design Note:**\nTop half of section: four skill pillars as cards in a row. Bottom half: tool logos displayed in a clean horizontal logo strip grouped by category.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\n\"No learning on the job\" directly addresses a real client fear \342\200\224 paying someone to figure things out at their expense. Real logos signal daily professional use. Four pillars make breadth feel structured rather than scattered.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 5 \342\200\224 CASE STUDIES\n\n**Section ID:** work\n\n**Section Label:**\nMy Work\n\n**Headline:**\nReal businesses. Real results.\n\n**Subline:**\nEvery brand I have worked with sells something physical. Here is what happened when they trusted me with their social media.\n\n---\n\n**Case Study 1 \342\200\224 Opara Motors**\nIndustry Tag: Automotive\nIcon: Car icon (or Opara Motors logo if supplied by client)\nServices Delivered: Content creation, video editing, social media management\n\nCard Headline:\nA car dealership that finally looked the part online.\n\nBody Copy:\nOpara Motors came to me with a social media presence that didn\'t reflect the quality of what they were selling. In one month, I took over their content \342\200\224 scripting, shooting direction, editing, and posting \342\200\224 and built a consistent visual identity around their inventory.\n\nThe result: 8,405 views, 6,722 people reached, and 1,000 new followers. In 30 days. For a car dealership that previously had next to no traction online.\n\nWhen your product costs what a car costs, your content needs to match that value. That was the brief. That was the result.\n\nMetrics (display as a 2x2 stat grid at the bottom of the card):\n- 8,405 Views\n- 6,722 Reach\n- 1,000 New Followers\n- 30 Days\n\n---\n\n**Case Study 2 \342\200\224 Omereugu Farms**\nIndustry Tag: Agriculture\nIcon: Crop or leaf icon (or brand logo if supplied by client)\nServices Delivered: Social media management, copywriting, video editing, strategic content\n\nCard Headline:\nBuilt from nothing. On purpose.\n\nBody Copy:\nOmereugu Farms had no social media presence at all. No followers, no content, no strategy. I built everything from the ground up \342\200\224 the content direction, the brand voice, the posting rhythm, the visual identity.\n\nStarting from zero is harder than it looks. There is no existing audience to lean on, no past content to learn from. Every follower is earned. We grew their TikTok to 50 followers and their Instagram to 12, with over 3,000 views across platforms in the early stages.\n\nThese are foundation numbers. What they represent is a brand that now exists online, speaks consistently, and is growing. The work here was not just execution \342\200\224 it was architecture.\n\nMetrics (display as a 2x2 stat grid at the bottom of the card):\n- 3,000+ Views\n- 50 TikTok Followers\n- 12 Instagram Followers\n- Built from 0\n\n---\n\n**Case Study 3 \342\200\224 Zext Ventures**\nIndustry Tag: Business Services\nIcon: Building icon (or brand logo if supplied by client)\nServices Delivered: Social media management, copywriting, video editing\n\nCard Headline:\nConsistent presence. Professional voice. Every week.\n\nBody Copy:\nZext Ventures needed a social media presence that matched the seriousness of their business. My job was to show up consistently, maintain a professional brand voice, and produce content that positioned them credibly in their space.\n\nOver two months I managed their platforms end to end \342\200\224 content creation, copy, video editing, and scheduling. 543 views and over 100 followers gained in a competitive space where most business service brands struggle to get any organic traction at all.\n\nNot every client needs to go viral. Some need to simply show up, look credible, and build steadily. That is exactly what we did.\n\nMetrics (display as a 2x2 stat grid at the bottom of the card):\n- 543 Views\n- 100+ New Followers\n- 2 Months\n- 3 Platforms\n\n---\n\n**Design Note:**\nThree cards side by side. Each card has the industry tag small at the top, the headline large, body copy in a lighter weight, and the 2x2 metric grid at the bottom. If the client supplies real screenshots or content mockups from these projects, display them as a visual thumbnail at the top of each card. If not, use the industry icon only. Do not fabricate mockup images.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\nEach case study tells a deliberately different story. Opara Motors is speed and impact. Omereugu Farms is about building from nothing, which positions Munachi as someone trusted at a brand\'s most vulnerable stage. Zext Ventures reframes modest numbers as intentional consistency. Together the three signal range across industries without undermining each other.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 6 \342\200\224 TESTIMONIALS\n\n**Section ID:** testimonials\n\n**Section Label:**\nWhat Clients Say\n\n**Headline:**\nDon\'t take my word for it.\n\n---\n\n**Testimonial Card 1**\nAvatar: Initials placeholder circle\nClient Name: [Opara Motors Client Name \342\200\224 to be filled before launch]\nRole: [Owner / Manager, Opara Motors]\nQuote: [Client quote to be inserted by Munachi before launch]\n\n**Testimonial Card 2**\nAvatar: Initials placeholder circle\nClient Name: [Omereugu Farms Client Name \342\200\224 to be filled before launch]\nRole: [Owner / Manager, Omereugu Farms]\nQuote: [Client quote to be inserted by Munachi before launch]\n\n**Testimonial Card 3**\nAvatar: Initials placeholder circle\nClient Name: [Zext Ventures Client Name \342\200\224 to be filled before launch]\nRole: [Owner / Manager, Zext Ventures]\nQuote: [Client quote to be inserted by Munachi before launch]\n\n**Design Note:**\nThree cards side by side. Each card has a large opening quotation mark, the quote text in italics at a lighter weight, client name in bold below, and their role in a smaller muted size beneath that. Leave an avatar circle for a headshot \342\200\224 use initials if no photo is provided. Do not fabricate any quote content. Placeholder text must be clearly marked for the client to replace before the site goes live.\n\n---\n\n## SECTION 7 \342\200\224 FINAL CTA\n\n**Section ID:** contact\n\n**Section Label:**\nLet\'s Work\n\n**Headline:**\nYou\'ve seen the work. You know what I do. Let\'s talk about what I can do for you.\n\n**Body Copy:**\nI take on a limited number of clients at a time so every brand I work with gets my full attention. If you are a physical business that is serious about social media, I want to hear from you.\n\n**Primary CTA Button:**\nHire Me\n(opens email client to orjimunachi5@gmail.com)\n\n**Secondary Line beneath button (smaller, muted):**\nor email me directly at orjimunachi5@gmail.com\n\n**Design Note:**\nFull-width section. Headline centered. Button centered beneath copy. Email address beneath button as a plain clickable mailto link. No form. No contact form. Direct email only \342\200\224 lowest possible friction.\n\n**Psychological Intent:**\n\"Limited number of clients\" creates scarcity without being manipulative and signals that her time is genuinely in demand. \"Serious about social media\" filters out tyre-kickers and price shoppers. The email sitting beneath the button removes every possible barrier between a decision and an action.\n\n---\n\n## NAVIGATION\n\nSticky nav.\n\nLeft: Name \342\200\224 Orji Munachi\nRight links: About, Services, Skills, Work, Contact\nFar right: Hire Me button\n\nAll links smooth-scroll to their respective sections.\n\n---\n\n## FOOTER\n\nLeft: Orji Munachi, Social Media Manager, 2026\nCenter or right: orjimunachi5@gmail.com\nSocial links: Instagram, LinkedIn (placeholders \342\200\224 client to supply profile URLs before launch)\n\nNo pricing. No copyright notice needed beyond the year.\n\n---\n\n## PRE-LAUNCH CHECKLIST FOR MUNACHI\n\nBefore the site goes live, replace the following:\n\n1. Supply brand visuals \342\200\224 colors, fonts, logo \342\200\224 from Google Stitch for the agent to apply\n2. Professional photo in the About section\n3. All three testimonial quotes and client names\n4. Brand logos for Opara Motors, Omereugu Farms, and Zext Ventures (if available)\n5. Real content screenshots or mockups for case study cards (if available)\n6. Instagram and LinkedIn profile URLs in the footer\n7. Confirm the Hire Me button correctly opens orjimunachi5@gmail.com\n\n---\n\n*Document prepared for AI agent handoff. All copy is final. Design notes are instructions, not suggestions. Branding to be applied by client after Google Stitch visuals are ready.*"
    }
