  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Single View**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the single-screen layout and ensuring it adheres to the design guide. I\'ve re-read the structural boundaries to make sure the single-view index exactly matches what the user will use.\n\n\n**Clarifying the Portfolio Structure**\n\nI\'ve refined the one-page portfolio structure. It\'s a scrollable resume, containing seven key sections: Hero, About, Services, Skills, Case Studies, Testimonials, and a Final CTA. I\'m focusing on the sticky navigation and footer, as well as an interactive preview checklist to guide Munachi through the final customization steps. I\'m currently conceptualizing how to best implement this checklist as a user-friendly overlay for easy pre-launch editing.\n\n\n**Conceptualizing the Launch Panel**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the \"Handoff & Live Customization Panel\" idea. I\'m imagining an elegant, interactive sidebar or floating control drawer called \"Munachi\'s Launch Center.\" It will let her preview real changes, replace placeholder details, and download or copy configuration. I can visualize all placeholders to replace. I\'m prioritizing user-friendliness and staying within the portfolio context. I\'m exploring an overlay to replace placeholders: Supply brand visuals, a photo, testimonial quotes, brand logos, and confirm links.\n\n\n**Refining the Customization**\n\nI\'m now integrating the editorial brutalism aesthetic as a floating \"Launch Checklist\" widget, readily accessible. I\'ve re-reviewed the user\'s styling requests, and the frontmatter\'s target palette aligns with a \"Vivid Portfolio Core\" theme. The ability to dynamically customize the secondary accent color is key; I\'m enabling toggling between Terracotta, Poison Green, Deep Cobalt, and Hot Pink within the panel.\n\n\n**Implementing Real-Time Color**\n\nI\'m now implementing the color picker for real-time adjustments. Placeholder images will use initials or geometric patterns; no stock photos. I\'m prioritizing SVG logos in a `/src/components/Logos.tsx` file for the skills and tools. It\'s time to build a robust file structure: I\'ll declare types in `/src/types.ts` and extract components to dedicated files, avoiding the monolithic approach.\n\n\n**Structuring the Core Components**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a robust component architecture. I\'m building out individual SVG icons for social media and marketing tools. I\'m also creating specific component files, breaking down the portfolio into distinct sections like Navigation, Hero, About, Services, Skills, Case Studies, Testimonials, Contact, and Footer. I\'m thinking `/src/components/LaunchCenter.tsx` will hold Munachi\'s interactive pre-launch checklist for easy edits and real-time previews.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/types.ts` to declare our data interfaces and state structures. This includes configurations for Orji\'s services, tools, case studies, testimonials, and contact details, ensuring strict type safety and enabling our interactive pre-launch editing center."
