  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining CSS Bindings**\n\nI\'ve made great strides in setting up the foundational CSS bindings! I\'ve now updated `/src/index.css` to properly define the fonts loaded from Google Fonts and the custom styling, which should give us a clean starting point. I\'m excited to see how this evolves as we move forward.\n\n\n**Refining CSS Styles**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into the styling process. I am examining the updated `/src/index.css` file closely. My plan is to incorporate variables, custom hover effects, a subtle grain overlay, and scroll animation support. I also intend to integrate key Editorial Brutalism utilities using Tailwind CSS v4 to enhance the design further.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will update `/src/index.css` to load Google Fonts (Anton, Work Sans, JetBrains Mono) and configure custom variables (accentColor, background) and Brutalist utility classes like borders and shadow offsets. This aligns with the visual design for high contrast and thick editorial shadows."
